messages:
Olivia: Heads-up  MegaCorp POC next Wed. They want a concise SE pack: websocket streaming SDK example with function/tool calling, pattern for batching function calls, schema-validated JSON output, short security answers (KMS, retention, DPA/SCC), and a pricing note showing burst vs sustained cost (hosted streaming vs Dedicated 2G). Who can take?

Ben: I can do the SDK + batching examples. Clarify: they want function calls batched (send multiple lookups in one call) or one-per-call? Batching reduces rtt.

Olivia: They prefer batching when editing multiple refs in a single save. Also need fallback when function-call batch partially fails.

Ben: OK. I'll prepare a small Node websocket example that sends a batch payload and shows handling partial results. Will include a REST curl fallback.

Harpreet: I'll draft the short security Q&A. Key asks flagged: are raw prompts stored, BYOK/KMS, region locks, audit log retention, SCCs, and ability to restrict function-call payload logging.

Katrina: I'll build the pricing delta. Note: show hosted per-1M tokens plus an example of burst pricing (short spikes) vs Dedicated steady state. Include math for 1M/5M/50M tokens and show 3-mo vs 12-mo commit.

Ben: Example snippet (Node, simplified):
```js
// websocket streaming with batch function calls
const ws = new RedwoodWS(URL, API_KEY);
ws.on('token', t => process.stdout.write(t));
ws.on('function_call_batch', async batch => {
  // batch = [{id, name, args}, ...]
  const results = await Promise.all(batch.map(async item => {
    try { return {id: item.id, result: await fetchCRM(item.args)}; }
    catch(e){ return {id: item.id, error: e.message}; }
  }));
  ws.sendFunctionBatchResults(results);
});
ws.send({model:'redwood-1-stream',stream:true,function_call:'batch',schema:{type:'object',properties:{records:{type:'array'}}}});
```

Ben: REST fallback (curl):
```bash
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -d '{"model":"redwood-1","prompt":"...","stream":false}'
```

Harpreet: Security draft: by default hosted request bodies are not persisted long-term; short debug logs may contain masked tokens. We support customer-managed keys (BYOK) on Private and enterprise hosted with KMS integration. Region locks available; data residency via Private. Audit logs retention configurable up to 36 months; immediate deletion APIs for enterprise contracts. SCCs/DPA: legal will provide connectors; function-call payload logging can be disabled per route. I'll flag SCC/DPA for legal.

Katrina: Pricing highlight: hosted streaming unit price (input+output) for conversation and editing flows; Dedicated 2G commit reduces unit cost for sustained usage. Example: 1M tokens hosted = $A, Dedicated-equivalent monthly cost = $B (~X% cheaper at steady load). I'll include burst calculator showing short-term spikes cost vs Dedicated amortized.

Ben: Also adding a tiny JSON-repair helper in repo for truncated JSON from streamed chunks, and a troubleshooting list: websocket auth 401, keepalive, partial JSON, large function batch throttling.

